# The package that holds Debian's archive signing keys, and its SHA-256.
# Everything else that goes into the image is checked against the keys in
# it, so the package itself is checked against the hash here rather than
# taken on the word of whichever server answered.
#
# Used where the machine building the image has no Debian keyring of its
# own that knows the release (Ubuntu, which is what CI runs on). When
# Debian publishes a newer keyring the old file leaves the archive and the
# build says so: take the new Filename and SHA256 from the
# debian-archive-keyring entry of
#   https://deb.debian.org/debian/dists/trixie/main/binary-all/Packages.xz
# and compare the hash with https://packages.debian.org/trixie/all/debian-archive-keyring/download
DEBIAN_KEYRING_DEB=pool/main/d/debian-archive-keyring/debian-archive-keyring_2025.1_all.deb
DEBIAN_KEYRING_SHA256=9ea7778e443144ca490668737a8ab22dd3e748bb99e805e22ec055abeb3c7fac
